 "verdict": "THE MECHANISM IS ONE, AND ITS SIGN IS SET BY SIZE: all four of X193's registered criteria pass at the smaller bodies. The bridge depends on the phase at fixed inflow - at F_local 0.03, the most crowded value with 44 classes, the ratio spans 0.00289-0.40363 (spread 0.40074, bar 0.05) - and the outcome follows it there, with the worlds above that value's median ratio fusing 0.5 more often than those below (Fisher p = 0.0001, bar 0.3). The logistic slope of fusion on the ratio over the 144 worlds is 4.854 (se 1.792, z = 2.71), positive with |z| >= 2. And the sign of the inflow relation is REVERSED against radius 6: the share rises from 0.0 at F_local 0.015 to 1.0 at 0.0375 (Spearman 0.413 over classes, 0.515 over the value means, against -0.378 and -0.833 at radius 6). So the same phase-and-bridge mechanism operates at both sizes, and the sign of the inflow-outcome relation is a property of the body size rather than of two unrelated laws: at radius 3 a stronger inflow fuses more, at radius 6 less. The census is one arm (radius 3 gap 10) with one representative world per phase class.",
 "criteria_note": "the Spearman against the inflow is +0.413 over classes and +0.515 over the nine value means, so the inherited monotone-decrease criterion of X192 does not apply at this arm and is not counted; X193 registered the reversal instead"
